{"archetypes":[{"name":"shell-ordering","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff introduces a strict result-env-before-side-effects ordering contract (route_write_result_env → route_emit_cancel_side_effects → route_emit_stdout_and_exit) that is both a functional requirement and verified by awk-based line-order pins in the test harness; a violation would silently emit side effects without a committed contract.","prompt_body":"Examine `skills/design/scripts/design-route.sh`'s new `emit_cancel_route_result` function and its three constituent helpers (`route_write_result_env`, `route_emit_cancel_side_effects`, `route_emit_stdout_and_exit`). Verify the call-chain ordering is always result-env first, then side effects, then stdout KV emit: check whether any code path can reach render/upsert side effects before `phase_driver_write_result_env` has been called and returned successfully. Check `render_cancel_summary`'s `_render_rc` local variable: it is set but `return 0` is unconditional — confirm this is intentional tolerance and that no downstream code ever reads a stale `$?` after the call. Verify the awk-based cancel_write_line / cancel_side_effects_line line-order pins in `scripts/test-design-structure.sh` actually capture the right function body (the awk anchors use `^emit_cancel_route_result()` which is the wrapper, not the helper functions) — confirm the pins land on `route_write_result_env` and `route_emit_cancel_side_effects` calls *inside* `emit_cancel_route_result`, not elsewhere. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"quiet-fd-bridge","focus_area":"code-robustness","weight":1,"rationale":"Both drivers now use the `[ \"${LARCH_QUIET_PID:-}\" = \"$$\" ]` / FD 4 conditional bridge for child process stderr; an unconditional `2>&4` when FD 4 is not open would crash the driver, and an inverted condition would leak diagnostics or drop them in the wrong mode.","prompt_body":"Inspect every occurrence of the quiet-child bridge (`[ \"${LARCH_QUIET_PID:-}\" = \"$$\" ]` / `>/dev/null 2>&4` / `>/dev/null`) in `skills/design/scripts/design-route.sh` (resume `write-design-current-env.sh` and both cancel `render-final-summary.sh` branches) and `skills/design/scripts/design-init-runparams.sh` (init `write-design-current-env.sh`). Verify that `$$` in each script refers to the script's own PID at execution time (not a subshell), that the non-quiet branch redirects only stdout and never touches FD 4, and that neither driver uses unconditional `2>&4`. Check whether `larch_quiet_init` (called in `design-route.sh`) opens FD 4 before the quiet branch is ever reached — if FD 4 is not open when the quiet branch runs, the `2>&4` redirect will fail under `set -e` or silently on some shells. Confirm the test pins `grep -Fq '[ \"${LARCH_QUIET_PID:-}\" = \"$$\" ]'` in `test-design-structure.sh` are anchored to the correct files. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"test-pin-migration","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff deletes several SKILL.md grep pins and replaces them with driver-file pins; any dropped invariant would silently weaken the regression harness without a test failure, since deleting a `contains` check is always green.","prompt_body":"Cross-reference every deleted pin in `scripts/test-design-structure.sh` (lines removed from the diff) against the newly added pins and verify one-to-one coverage: specifically the lifecycle/archival reject banner text (`issue title starts with managed lifecycle marker`, `issue title matches archival report-prefix`), the reentry-guard session-cache banner (`**⚠ /design: refusing spurious re-entry — guard=session-cache`), the delete-path hint, and the resume `_wdce_resume_args` / repo-forwarding / `_wdce_resume_rc` / failure-message pins. Confirm that the new pins assert the same semantic literals (not weaker partial matches) and that the scoped check for `_wdce_resume_args` inside `DESIGN_ROUTE_SH` cannot accidentally pass by matching a comment rather than a live code path. Check whether the removed assertion `grep -Fq '_wdce_resume_args' \"$DESIGN_ROUTE_SH\" || fail` uses a plain `grep -Fq` (exact literal) or could match a commented-out line. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"larch-errf-format","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The new `larch_errf` call for the reentry-guard banner passes six positional arguments to a format string with six `%s` placeholders and a trailing `\\n`; a count mismatch or wrong variable binding would produce a garbled or truncated operator message that is the primary cancellation signal.","prompt_body":"Locate the `larch_errf` invocation inside `route_emit_cancel_side_effects` in `skills/design/scripts/design-route.sh` for the `cancel-reentry-guard` branch. Count the format-string `%s` placeholders and the actual arguments passed (`$ISSUE`, `$CLAUDE_PID`, `$MARKER_AGE`, `$MARKER_TTL`, `$MARKER_REMAINING`, `$DESIGN_REENTRY_MARKER_PATH`) and confirm they match in number and position — in particular verify `$CLAUDE_PID` appears where the old SKILL.md code used `$PPID` (the plan says to use `$CLAUDE_PID`) and that `$MARKER_REMAINING` (computed from `MARKER_TTL - MARKER_AGE`) is correctly floored to 0 before the `larch_errf` call. Check that the trailing `\\n` in the format string is handled correctly by `larch_errf` (i.e., whether `larch_errf` adds its own newline — double-newline would leave a blank line in the operator output). Also verify that `DESIGN_REENTRY_MARKER_PATH` is populated before `route_emit_cancel_side_effects` is called (it is set via `design_reentry_marker_path "$ISSUE" "$CLAUDE_PID" 2>/dev/null || true` — confirm this assignment happens before `emit_cancel_route_result`). Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
